  },
  "ingredients": [
    "40 ounce beef stew meat",
    "3 cup brewed coffee",
    "1 cup beef broth",
    "4 1/2 ounce cremini mushrooms",
    "2/3 cup dry red wine",
    "1 medium onion",
    "3 tablespoon coconut oil",
    "2 tablespoon capers",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon black pepper"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Cube all stew meat into bite-size chunks. Cut off excess grit. Season with salt and pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice onions, mushrooms, and mince the garlic.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring coconut oil to its smoking point in a pan on the stove.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brown the beef in batches that don’t overcrowd the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "As you finish a batch, remove the beef to a plate and continue with the remaining batch (or batches).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the beef is finished, start sauteing the onion, mushrooms, and minced garlic in the remaining fat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the onions are translucent add coffee, beef stock, red wine, and capers.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix everything together well, then add your beef. Bring the mixture to a boil. Once mixture is boiling, turn the stove to low and cover the pan with a lid. Let this cook for 3 hours on low.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/coffee-wine-beef-stew-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you want to, you can let this simmer without a lid for 30 minutes after the 3 hour mark. This will help reduce the liquids, if you want a thicker sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/coffee-wine-beef-stew/#wprm-recipe-50897-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
